      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. This dose is about twice that limit. Metformin at high doses raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled ceiling.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily** with meals, which is a common regimen.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do need more than the labeled maximum, please take that up with pharmacy or the attending. I can't enter it based on a verbal confirmation."
      }
     ],
